WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.045 --> 00:00:02.462
(beatboxing)

00:00:10.186 --> 00:00:12.103
- I'm Pops, the mentor.

00:00:13.415 --> 00:00:15.832
(beatboxing)

00:00:16.989 --> 00:00:21.572
- And I'm I'm I'm I'm I'm
Nicole Paris, the apprentice.

00:00:23.375 --> 00:00:25.792
(beatboxing)

00:00:26.798 --> 00:00:31.131
- Beatboxing is just simply
making sounds with your mouth.

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:33.140
Making music with your mouth.

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:36.067
When beatboxing came to St.
Louis in the early ‘80s,

00:00:36.067 --> 00:00:39.326
it was always about
emulating what the DJ did.

00:00:39.326 --> 00:00:43.259
So I just thought of perfecting
my skill as I got older

00:00:43.259 --> 00:00:47.053
and then, my wife, she
gets pregnant with Nicole.

00:00:47.053 --> 00:00:49.876
So I would beatbox up against the belly

00:00:49.876 --> 00:00:52.575
and Nicole would start
twisting and you would see

00:00:52.575 --> 00:00:55.679
my wife's belly almost like (beatboxing).

00:00:55.679 --> 00:00:58.055
She liked it, she thought
it was funny and cute.

00:00:58.055 --> 00:01:00.610
And then, as Nicole got
bigger in the belly,

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:02.106
it wasn't cute no more.

00:01:02.106 --> 00:01:06.009
- At the age of 13,
was my first talent show.

00:01:06.009 --> 00:01:07.989
I just went home and I said,

00:01:07.989 --> 00:01:10.149
"Pops, I just joined a talent show,

00:01:10.149 --> 00:01:11.725
"you're going to
teach me how to beatbox."

00:01:11.725 --> 00:01:15.260
He taught me how to hold a
mic, taught me how to breath,

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:17.444
taught me the basic beats.

00:01:17.444 --> 00:01:19.075
I went to the talent show and did that.

00:01:19.075 --> 00:01:20.439
They made me mad at the talent show,

00:01:20.439 --> 00:01:22.678
they was clapping off-beat.

00:01:22.678 --> 00:01:26.049
And they was like (slow clapping).

00:01:26.049 --> 00:01:30.161
I then started to add my own
thing to what he thought me.

00:01:30.161 --> 00:01:32.381
- One night, I came home from work

00:01:32.381 --> 00:01:34.425
and as I'm walking in the door...

00:01:34.425 --> 00:01:37.163
(beatboxing)

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:40.062
I heard her making all
these strange noises.

00:01:40.062 --> 00:01:41.708
I had to tell her, like, “That's not beatboxing.

00:01:41.708 --> 00:01:43.922
"Nah, don't do that, that's corny."

00:01:43.922 --> 00:01:45.872
- I was like, (record screech) "what?"

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:48.882
- This is when I had to
realize and tell myself,

00:01:48.882 --> 00:01:50.685
“Look, this is what she wants to do."

00:01:50.685 --> 00:01:53.102
(beatboxing)

00:01:54.605 --> 00:01:58.169
- Me and Pops, we
beatbox anywhere, all day.

00:01:58.169 --> 00:01:59.228
- It don't even make a difference.

00:01:59.228 --> 00:02:00.061
- No, it really don't.

00:02:00.061 --> 00:02:03.864
We beatbox while cooking, barbershop, ...

00:02:03.864 --> 00:02:05.921
- When we ready to
beatbox, it literally ...

00:02:05.921 --> 00:02:06.947
- It happens.

00:02:06.947 --> 00:02:07.780
- It doesn't matter.

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:10.080
If you go to her YouTube channel,

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:12.413
you will see us sitting down, beatboxing,

00:02:12.413 --> 00:02:16.343
and to some folks, it can
look like a competition.

00:02:16.343 --> 00:02:18.281
- We're not really battling, it's just ...

00:02:18.281 --> 00:02:20.785
- It's just jam sessions,
just us having fun.

00:02:20.785 --> 00:02:23.640
This is how I bond with
my child even though 160 million people will

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:27.140
be like, “Pops, you lost.”

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:29.861
"Pop, loser!"

00:02:29.861 --> 00:02:34.385
I want her to be the best.
I want her to, to outdo me.

00:02:34.385 --> 00:02:37.037
Not in outdo me, like, as in a
battle, but I want her to

00:02:37.037 --> 00:02:40.705
just, just continue to grow
and add to beatboxing.

00:02:40.705 --> 00:02:43.955
(soft music and chime)

